#### Beamforming

Linearly constrained minimum variance (LCMV) beamformer spatial filters
({{ ref('VanVeen1997', 'Van Veen, B. D., van Drongelen, W., Yuchtman, M., & Suzuki, A. (1997). Localization of brain electrical activity via linearly constrained minimum variance spatial filtering. IEEE Transactions on Biomedical Engineering, 44(9), 867–880. doi:10.1109/10.623056') }})
were computed using MNE-Python.

{% if s.settings.data_cov_source == 'continuous' %}
The data covariance matrix was estimated from the continuous recording using automatic covariance estimation.
{% elif s.settings.data_cov_source == 'epoched' %}
The data covariance matrix was estimated from the epoched data using automatic covariance estimation.
{% elif s.settings.data_cov_source == 'provided' %}
A precomputed data covariance matrix was used.
{% endif %}

{% if s.settings.noise_cov_source == 'empty_room' %}
The noise covariance matrix was estimated from a preprocessed empty-room recording.
{% elif s.settings.noise_cov_source == 'nearest_empty_room' %}
The noise covariance matrix was estimated from the nearest-in-time preprocessed empty-room recording.
{% elif s.settings.noise_cov_source == 'provided' %}
A precomputed noise covariance matrix was used.
{% elif s.settings.noise_cov_source == 'ad_hoc' %}
An ad-hoc noise covariance matrix was used.
{% elif s.settings.noise_cov_source == 'none' %}
No noise covariance matrix was used.
{% endif %}

{% if s.settings.pick_ori == 'max-power' %}
At each source location, the orientation maximizing source power was selected.
{% elif s.settings.pick_ori == 'normal' %}
Source orientations were constrained normal to the cortical surface.
{% elif s.settings.pick_ori == 'vector' %}
The three source-orientation components were retained separately.
{% endif %}

{% if s.settings.weight_norm == 'nai' %}
Beamformer weights were normalized using the Neural Activity Index (NAI)
{%- elif s.settings.weight_norm == 'unit-noise-gain' %}
Beamformer weights were normalized to unit noise gain
{%- elif s.settings.weight_norm == 'unit-noise-gain-invariant' %}
Beamformer weights were normalized using rotation-invariant unit noise gain
{%- elif s.settings.weight_norm is none %}
No beamformer weight normalization was applied
{%- endif %}, with a regularization parameter of {{ s.settings.reg }}.

{% if s.settings.reduce_rank %}
The beamformer denominator rank was reduced by one at each source location.
{% endif %}